        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: محرر",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "محرر — muḥarrir — \"an editor\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "يعمل خالي محررا في مجلة. yaʿmalu khālī muḥarriran fī majalla. My uncle works as an editor at a magazine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The verbal noun تحرير is editing: the editorial office is قسم التحرير."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "محرر (muḥarrir) is built on the native Arabic root ḥ-r-r (Lane), \"to be free\", the root of ḥurr, free. Form II ḥarrara means \"to set free\" and \"to write a text out clean\"; muḥarrir is its participle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
